{
  "id": "Compound::DB00511 - Gene::481",
  "verbalization": "Acetyldigitoxin exhibits a strong binding interaction with Fxyd2, which is involved in potassium transport and sodium-potassium exchange, both of which are associated with the activity of Atp1b1. This binding suggests a potential mechanism by which Acetyldigitoxin may influence Atp1b1 function. The evidence from multiple paths indicates that Acetyldigitoxin may modulate Atp1b1 through a shared pathway involving Fxyd2, which is a key component of the sodium-potassium-exchanging Atpase. The consistent involvement of Fxyd2 in both potassium-transporting and sodium-potassium-exchanging activities, and its role in the participation of Atp1b1, supports a mechanistic link between Acetyldigitoxin and Atp1b1. The high scores from the paths suggest that this relationship is well-supported by the available data, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct effect of Acetyldigitoxin on Atp1b1.",
